{
  "id": "pokemon-the-first-movie-theatrical-release",
  "name": "Pokémon: The First Movie theatrical release",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Pokémon: The First Movie opened in North American cinemas in November 1999, and select theaters gave away four exclusive cards, Electabuzz, Mewtwo, Pikachu and Dragonite, Wizards Black Star Promos 2 to 5, handed out in random order over the weeks the film played there. Each has a gold \"Kids WB Presents Pokémon The First Movie\" stamp on its picture, and the packs held an insert advertising the new Pokémon League. One sheet was never stamped and another went through the stamping upside down, so each card also exists with no stamp and with an inverted one.\n\nThree of the four had come out in Japan first: Electabuzz with the 1997 Official Card File, Mewtwo in the Pocket Monsters Official Fan Book, and Dragonite from All Nippon Airways' Get in a Jet! campaign. In 2002 all four came back as \"classic\" promos in the Pokémon League's third year, Energize Your Game.",
